<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Description">Description</span></h2>
<p>Version 1.0 of the toolset had a bug in ExcelProcessor.exe that caused row IDs to become inaccurate when larger than 8 million (reportedly 2<sup>23</sup>-1, or 8388607, if you'd like a more exact number). This was due to the integer being converted into a float internally, losing precision in the process.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Workarounds">Workarounds</span></h2>
<p>It was possible to work around the problem by manually editing the GDA file using the GFF editor. However, the bug in ExcelProcessor has been fixed in subsequent releases of the toolset.
</p>
